mi-formal community engagement — consistent with project discussions.\n\n---\n\n**6) Documentation of external help acceptance**  \n→ **YES.** The sign itself is official documentation. It states the project is “implemented by” Kiribati ministries “with the generous support of” USAID. This is formal acknowledgment and acceptance of external help. The fact that the sign is erected publicly and maintained (visible across multiple frames) further confirms institutional and community-level acceptance.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence and Context:**\n\n- The video sequence moves from a community gathering (frames 1–2, 10–11) → to a village scene with a project sign (frames 3–6) → to a close-up of the sign detailing the USAID-backed project (frames 7–9).\n- This progression suggests a narrative arc: local community life → visible evidence of external aid → explicit documentation of that aid.\n- The presence of the sign in public view and the community meeting imply that the islanders are not only aware of but are actively engaged with the external support.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe evidence across the frames — particularly the explicit project sign with USAID and SPREP logos, the mention of implementation by local ministries, and the context of community gatherings — **clearly indicates that the islanders have accepted help from the outside.**\n\nTherefore, the correct answer to “Did the islanders accept help from the outside?” is **‘0’ (Yes)**.\n\n✅ **Answer ‘1’ (No) is incorrect.**'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-11 (11 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/frames/frame_1632.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/frames/frame_1633.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/frames/frame_1634.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/frames/frame_1635.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/frames/frame_1636.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/TZ0j6kr4ZJ0/f